"rifaximin": "Rifaximin suggests cirrhosis with prior hepatic encephalopathy, or IBS with diarrhea. New confusion in these patients can reflect missed doses, GI bleeding, infection or constipation.",
"diphenoxylate-atropine": "Diphenoxylate-atropine (Lomotil) suggests chronic diarrhea. In a child ingestion, anticholinergic signs can come first and respiratory depression can be delayed many hours, and naloxone reverses the opioid effect.",
