"fact": "Rethymic is made from thymus tissue removed from infants having heart surgery, processed and cultured into slices, then surgically implanted into the thigh muscle of children born without a thymus. The child's own immature T cells travel to the implant and learn to work there, which usually takes 6 to 12 months. The FDA approved Rethymic in 2021 for immune reconstitution in congenital athymia.",
